WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
"In the days when the spinning-wheels
hummed busily in the farmhouses",

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.950
strange pale men walked the country lanes.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.700
Each is bent under a heavy bag.

4
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.820
The shepherd's dog barks as one
passes, dark against the winter sunset.

5
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:21.710
Far away, in a busy town, Silas's
little chapel stands among the rooftops.

6
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.420
Time-lapse: a factory
rises, and the chapel fades.

7
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:30.910
So why does Eliot swap Silas's
old chapel for a factory?

8
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.120
In this mission, you'll meet the travelling
linen-weavers who open the novel.

9
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.770
You'll see how power looms in factories
made hand weavers' wages collapse by the

10
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.110
1820s.

11
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.070
And you'll explore Raveloe, a village
that the coach-horn never reaches.

12
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Your mission: explain why Eliot
replaces the chapel with a factory.
